{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For they have loosened the bowstring</b> — the opposite of \"my bow is set in my hand.\"" "<b>And the bridle because of impoverishment</b> — at first they had a bridle, like beasts, because of my fear; but now they have cast off the bridle because of impoverishment. And some say: for the old horse they remove the bridle from it and abandon it, and grown men and children make sport of it. And so: \"and the bridle because of impoverishment\" — and this is far-fetched."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:00.664149805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}